,"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#4-use-components","content":"Import any component and use it in the application."},"460":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#typescript-support","content":"Hummingbird React is written in TypeScript and includes type definitions for all components. Component props are fully typed and available on each component's namespace, so no additional `@types` packages are needed."},"461":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#customization","content":"All components accept a `className` prop. Custom classes are merged with the component classes, so Tailwind utility classes can be used to adjust any component."},"462":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#customization","content":"For theme-level changes such as colors and spacing, Hummingbird provides global and component-specific CSS variables. See the Customize section for details."},"463":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction"},"464":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","content":"Welcome to the Hummingbird React documentation. It is an open-source React component library built on Hummingbird CSS and Radix UI primitives."},"465":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#what-is-hummingbird-react","content":