ponents with a consistent, typed API."},"472":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#why-hummingbird-react","content":"Ships accessible behavior out of the box through Radix UI primitives."},"473":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#why-hummingbird-react","content":"Reduces reliance on large sets of Tailwind utility classes."},"474":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#why-hummingbird-react","content":"Offers component variants through simple props such as `variant`, `color`, and `size`."},"475":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#why-hummingbird-react","content":"Supports full customization using the `className` prop and Tailwind utility classes."},"476":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#why-hummingbird-react","content":"Provides global and component-specific CSS variables for deeper configuration."},"477":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#why-hummingbird-react","content":"Includes complete TypeScript definitions for every component."},"478":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/introduction#why-hummingbird-react","content":"Supports tree shaking through per-component imports."},"479":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/introduction-15","page_i